B2gdzdr5I7G1cpnyyHJjXX1j0711g2s6St">here you are</a>.</p>=0A<p>I think of t=
he sommelier thing every time I see a new cool web component, especially if=
 it=E2=80=99s got that =E2=80=9Cstand-alone=E2=80=9D quality where you can =
just link it up and use it immediately. Here=E2=80=99s an example! <a href=
=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/k1srBR2naQtqbn90CaTXFw~~/AABEfhA~/4Fa=
fW1KmeJxzcpQzSiXt8tBTEGPEi4BXncDCoSEQwqGsQhayg-wMy9D_TNIvMz5-J2J-3fXR17Dao3=
O26IgGWIijCRS3e8I4wGQrGMVuoWNGDhqvaqKB8I8K8UR_KWGm">spoilerjs</a>. All you =
do is:</p>=0A<p><code>import 'spoilerjs/spoiler-span'; </code></p>=0A<p>The=
n you can use the web component to wrap whatever, which hides it with these=
 cool particles.</p>=0A<pre><code class=3D"html">&lt;spoiler-span&gt;It's a=
 sled.&lt;/spoiler-span&gt;=0A</code></pre>=0A<p>Click it, and the particle=
s disperse, <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/GVkJ_vmCXSiEA2BLfi=
RIhA~~/AABEfhA~/tdUiXZNSJTRH9ddRqwOr8p-TzenLv_AQvai6FOlkzdYVhfpuJm7YIyC5cPj=
5vEwZY4_fCBA2Mizd7MtVnIlORDHSYYPlLDY-iec2y8vPjbh3tDatOACDPHvCkEQuLk56yajh-a=
bJS18nMzNdmrGHH5-NmpfOysq_zNR1zyBaUPg5Sd-8RrhVkEAKGwUzqBRO">revealing the s=
poiler</a>.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codep=
enassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-s=
park/rosebud_spoiler.png" alt=3D"A particle spoiler indicator, overlaid ove=
r repetitions of the word 'Rosebud'. " width=3D"250"/>=0A<hr />=0A<p>I=E2=
=80=99ve seen TWO games that:</p>=0A<ul>=0A<li>Involve horses.</li>=0A<li>U=
se the .horse TLD</li>=0A</ul>=0A<p>I dunno, just seems notable.</p>=0A<p>T=
he game at <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/LFOhdacpj-vaiabXxH-=
QDw~~/AABEfhA~/K4teUClMYWWbnDPZJrxZqcq-jKP2Fus05So4osfXM2oMRnJCyThE_EmUtB_n=
L-slNVcJGAx3JNPW6KUE4ovYFMCvUEexOnpsAvBCD-ppxphGgM4WhHJCJonFamxYksJo">enclo=
se.horse</a> has you building walls to enclose areas that yield the most ar=
ea/points. The =E2=80=9Cgame=E2=80=9D at <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmai=
l2.com/f/a/HiGee1-VTMluQcE2flQxtA~~/AABEfhA~/RqnOHpQgV01qSFoJDDPK1Z2pWiHhfO=
Czj2pavyLYADh7Qq3GHcTesRmgAQGLG5EboGdjrphHyRC5yXwZxh48UscV7hY04HdrJTg7OehWA=
RTErRBJwZ0J3SVWXHVgDuGt">gradient.horse</a> has you drawing your own horse =
(and horse parts) that then goes to join a parade of other rather happy hor=
ses.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenasset=
s.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/gr=
adient_horse.png" alt=3D"Screenshot from the game gradient horse showing Ch=
ris' ok drawing of a horse." width=3D"300"/>=0A<hr />=0A<p>I=E2=80=99m hone=
stly not sure if liquid glass is still interesting or not (I suspect intere=
st has waned), but I do quite like this generator thingy: <a href=3D"https:=
//go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/iaeYEgh7Bp87-i4fg4Zl6g~~/AABEfhA~/517BZi09peUJy=
MkG4uBfUdCWC_3-Yzj4Y--IXmWMmIXEZLRhYxWblGI9iqx8o57dSxrRNztgjpCk8JoBcC4iCZ1y=
RRD7lJ9LoSJBhZyrcNgyQPzz5RyeNioLvYaU6liw">Aether CSS</a>. I like it because=
 there are lots of options for the final look. Sometimes it=E2=80=99s frost=
ed, and sometimes it=E2=80=99s not. Sometimes there is a lot of distortion;=
 sometimes, a little. Sometimes the light hits harder than in other example=
s. There is no right or wrong (until you can=E2=80=99t read the text, then =
it=E2=80=99s wrong).</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-ass=
ets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/=
codepen-spark/liquid-glass-comp.png" alt=3D"Side-by-side comparison of fros=
ted vs. liquid glass effects. " width=3D"500"/>=0A<hr />=0A<p>The Web Audio=
 API remains extremely cool. But sometimes you just need a little audio fil=
e of a neat little sound. <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/F93W=
B_FuGdITXWDEluIdrw~~/AABEfhA~/R0-nMtpLqy7S0k_P9CS2ErytkCNbXM22KAD_zAlxgNlfs=
7gf7R_ugSAf26JTt1mV6ldzPCeojE2dT4KdZkuin6XE4LtHUiv0mjw6fw04MxI~">jsfxr</a> =
is kinda both.</p>=0A<blockquote><p>Jsfxr is an online 8 bit sound maker an=
d sfx generator. All you need to make retro sound effects with jsfxr is a w=
eb browser. It=E2=80=99s a JavaScript port of the original <a href=3D"https=
://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/YApNqtArpLYT1sQd_ESxkg~~/AABEfhA~/GRd7e0A-zCIV=
G4_rs8FTVVLXvnr8D_MyAztZyheryYR3ah5DoRkm2B8GpHp2yQJtv3Sfle_XcsSR3dHHzvUhjqb=
G2YWFRleIcYgAKi5qnrvTj3iloOtevhYIVDFqyO88uwDcSNTNkzAXgVmu3fl4Tw~~">sfxr</a>=
 by DrPetter. You can also use it as a <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2=
.com/f/a/KNkXmEz1y3yOA3co5jZG0w~~/AABEfhA~/s-1PjGpmryb1wNdC4u3NREAGYcXhUVy=
o8U_GFRFHWU1XkT60RV4Vmqrns3a9IAWH0X2OxHYw22yV-fHFjBaPmi9h2ztCFQvjzYXrTY23gp=
aqQi3CwyrpJ-KwdSquu9y1CDniOdtYOwV28hWwupefUw~~">JavaScript library</a> for =
playing and rendering sfxr sound effects in your games.</p></blockquote>=0A=
<p>You adjust all these levers to make small sounds, then can output the so=
und to use without any API or library usage. The <strong>random</strong> bu=
tton is very fun.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets=
.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/co=
depen-spark/jsfxr.png" alt=3D"Screenshot of the jsfxr sound generator inter=
face displaying various options for sound creation including settings for w=
aveform selection, envelope adjustments, frequency modulation, and effects =
like flanger and filters" width=3D"500"/>=0A<hr/>=0A<p>Weird aside: remembe=
r when we used to have the term <em>adaptive</em>, as an alternative to <em=
>responsive</em>=3F As best I can remember, it meant a site that had <code>=
@media</code> query breakpoints that changed layout, but the layouts were r=
ather fixed after that, as opposed to the fluid grids of <em>responsive des=
ign</em>. The jsfxr site is adaptive.</p>=0D=0A                          =
